ll end at end of line, no visible change. Use left direction .05: end x=33 within word, selection shrinks to \"o\" maybe; screenshot should change. Let's try on current Notes? Current selection isn't active now; content has indent. We can use Notes text with long press \"Notes\" title? But keyboard. Maybe easier use current Notes, long press \"See\"? Let's not.\n\nCould test on Notes content, but want multi-line. Hmm.\n\nPotential trick to multi-line selection: Use built-in search? Search action opens dialog; typing query can select match? In Markor, search highlights occurrences but not selection. No.\n\nCould use \"Select all\" then cut, then paste? Not.\n\nCould use accessibility \"Select all\" plus one \"DPAD_RIGHT\"? When entire text selected and no shift, arrow collapses to end. Not.\n\nMaybe use alternatekeyboard \"ctrl\" via hardware key not available. `press_key` supports specific keys only; maybe `KEYCODE_SHIFT_LEFT`? Key enum includes maybe no. Could try press_key(\"SHIFT_LEFT\")? Might fail. Or string \"Shift\" not in enum. No documentation list uses \"...\".\n\nMaybe we can type text via type_text with Unicode combining? Not selection.\n\nCould use long-press on word then drag handle with `swipe` starting slightly above handle center. Let's test on Notes with a simple document. But Notes content now 9 spaces line, select \"Notes\" heading. Need hide keyboard first? currently open. We can long press \"Notes\" x maybe 100,y243. Then screenshot."}
