{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha! This is bug! Output:\n```\n# **Notes**\n****\n**See [the guide](https://example.com/guide)**\n****\n```\nExpected bold each affected line:\n```\n**# Notes**\n****\n**See [the guide](https://example.com/guide)**\n```\nor maybe blank lines should not be bolded / no trailing empty. The selection started on \"# Notes\" whole line? Actually select all includes trailing newline. Affected lines computed from start/end selection include empty line between and trailing newline, each blank line got `****`. Also heading line got `# **Notes**` not `**# Notes**`! Wait long-press Bold with select all on text with heading: selection likely only the word \"Notes\" not all? We tapped Select all, but elements no visible selection info. The result \"# **Notes**\\n****\\n**See...**\\n****\" indicates first line applied bold around just \"Notes\" (not whole line), while line 3 entire \"See...\" bold, plus blank lines got `****`. Hmm why \"# **Notes**\" not \"**# Notes**\"? If select all applied, first line should `**# Notes**`. Instead marker inserted after \"# \" and before \"Notes\". That suggests selection range started after \"# \" not at line start. Maybe tap Select all didn't actually select all? The long press selected \"# Notes\" word \"Notes\"? Select all tap may have failed? Observe doesn't show selection. But result indicates selection start at \"Notes\" (after \"# \") and end at file end including trailing newline. So selection was from word \"Notes\" (long press selection) not all. Did Select all not apply due tap? In prior Single test, Select all applied all and result `**alpha**\\n**beta**\\n**gamma**` included first line from start. Hmm maybe because in Notes long press selected \"Notes\" word and we tapped \"Select all\" but due landscape? Wait element 64 was Select all; tap should. But result not select all. Could be selection start is start of selected word, end of doc? Maybe \"Select all\" action only extended end? No.\n\nLet's inspect the output carefully. It seems hold gesture wraps each **line segment affected between selectionStart and selectionEnd**, but if selection start mid-line, first line only subset is bolded? User description \"affected lines are now computed from the start and end of the selection range\" means per-line markers around selected range? Could expected behavior be`# **Notes**` for partial first line and full remaining lines, plus blank lines? Hmm.\n\nWait our result:\n- Line1 `# **Notes**` (original \"# Notes\"; only word Notes bold)\n- Line2 `****` (original blank; weird)\n- Line3 `**See [the guide](https://example.com/guide)**`\n- Line4 `****` (original trailing newline? bold empty line)\nIf selection was entire document, line1 should have `**# Notes**`, not `# **Notes**`. So likely selection started at start of word \"Notes\" and ended at end of text. Yet line3 and line4 got markers. How could selection start at word Notes and end at doc end? Maybe Select all action is not implemented and selection remained word Notes; but hold gesture then affected lines from selection start to selection end only, which would just `# **Notes**`; not line3. Unless selection end default at end? Hmm.\n\nMaybe long-press Bold always processes from start of current selected word to **end of document**? That would be an obvious bug. But our Single test after select all had selection maybe entire doc (long press on alpha then Select all) and all lines got markers. We didn't verify whether first line was fully bolded vs only alpha; result `**alpha**` because line only alpha. So cannot distinguish.\n\nThe blank-line markers `****` are suspicious. Expected behavior for affected lines maybe all lines from start to end including blank lines? If selection from beginning to end, bold each line. For blank lines, perhaps should not insert `****`? But maybe Markor's logic intentionally bolds blank lines? Unlikely.\n\nAlso trailing newline: line4 `****` indicates end selection at after trailing newline creates a blank final line and adds bold markers. That is likely the bug \"affected lines computed from start and end of selection range\" maybe off-by-one causing extra line. But title says fix; in this build it's buggy maybe intentionally.\n\nLet's reproduce more cleanly using a one-line selection vs select all; our Select all may not have worked. Let's check with screenshot selection before Bold? We didn't. We need controlled. We can use Ctrl+A perhaps the \"Select all\" action; likely did select all. But result first line partial is weird.\n\nWait original line was \"# Notes\". If long-press selected \"Notes\" only, then tap Select all maybe selects all actually. But after style action, maybe the logic doesn't use `selectionStart`/`selectionEnd` for the first line? It could use \"start of selected text\" incorrectly because `selectionStart` is at \"N\" while selectionEnd at doc end; if Select all didn't include preceding \"# \" somehow? The TextView `getSelectionStart()` after Select all should be 0, unless Select all failed. Could check selection by observing highlighted text screenshot after tapping Select all. Let's do another test with a known original simple content \"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\" (trailing newline) and explicitly use Select all; screenshot before hold to know selection. We'll use Single or Notes. Need restore anyway. Better use Notes again after reload original. Type content \"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\" clear. Long press alpha then Select all, screenshot selection. Then long press Bold, observe output. This will isolate trailing newline and whether select all. Let's do.\n\nFirst reload current mutated Notes? Use menu > Reload to original then type test. Could just clear type test. We'll restore original later. Use type_text clear true \"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\". Then long press alpha (x? keyboard open) and select all. Then screenshot before. Then long press Bold. Let's do."}
