{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restoration done likely. Need verify Shopping, Notes, Single contents persist. We can open each maybe after tests. Shopping timestamp 2:59; content should be original. Notes 3:00 original. Single 2:59. Good.\n\nNeed reset Settings Auto-format? We toggled it back on for Shopping. But wait we had disabled Auto-format and then re-enabled before strong emphasis; yes. After restoring Shopping via clear type on Auto-format on? Let's check sequence: We disabled Auto-format, typed original exact. Then did select all test. Then restored Shopping with clear exact **while Auto-format still off**. Then re-enabled. So final state on. Good. Notes auto-format maybe had default on (we didn't change per-file). Fine.\n\nTab width reset 4. Yes.\n\nNow test preview code block once more after restoration? We already did. Need maybe retrieve copy button bug maybe it's real but dev unconfirmed. Could attempt a different view mode route to see if copy button stays blank. We can open Single but original gamma, no code. We'd have to edit again and restore. Already enough.\n\nMaybe more reliable bug in preview: The Copy button being invisible could be confirmed by screenshot with \"Copy\" absent. If we want to refile, maybe specify \"the control is a blank white circle on the code block; accessibility says Copy.\" We did. It was rejected. Maybe because first screenshot may lag; but we waited 3s and re-entered, still blank. Could be actual theme in our environment only due \"follow system dark mode\"? Maybe device light mode. The developer couldn't reproduce perhaps because their copy button uses dark mode? But same device. Hmm.\n\nMaybe this is a **real seeded bug** but developer's reply \"could not reproduce\" means we need mention a simpler exact reproduction: use **existing** file content? None has code block. Need edit a file, which dev may not. Maybe because we changed code block and auto-saved? They might check after restart etc. Still.\n\nCould use **Quick