Let's test **multi-line code block copy** placement: Copy button at top-right aligned first line; okay.\n\nLet's test **inline code** preview: not relevant.\n\nNow tab width dialog: maybe after all tests, our setting 4 restored. Need verify by long-press Indent showing options; no check mark but okay.\n\nCould there be a bug in dialog **applied directly to open editor** only after some action? We tested. Maybe choosing 8 changed width but the editor's **existing tab stop guide**? no.\n\nPotential bug if cancel after choice? not.\n\nLet's test **enumeration button** on existing ordered list line. Neighboring Unordered list converts toggling appropriately. Enumeration at cursor in a numbered list may incorrectly insert bold markers. Already.\n\nMaybe ordered list button when no selection in empty line inserts \"1. ****\" with **bold around placeholder**, which is exactly bug. We can report clearly. Confirmed. Good.\n\nPotential **Check list** button could also have wrong insertion logic? It has \"Check list\"; if tapped inserts \"- [ ] \"? Maybe not.\n\nPotential **Date and time** button with no selection appends current datetime. Fine.\n\nPotential **Horizontal line** inserts \"\\n***\\n\" or \"---\"; maybe okay.\n\nPotential **Special Key** dialog actions maybe.\n\nLet's test **Bold toolbar button on selected word** (not long press) quickly, to compare with strong hold. We did long press only; but area formatting toolbar includes normal bold. Our earlier long press on selected word produced same as normal? We can test selected word via long press then tap (not long) Bold. Single? We can use Notes original, select word \"Notes\", tap Bold. Output \"# **Notes**\" expected. That's fine.\n\nMaybe **enumeration button** long press? It may strong-emphasize? no.\n\nLet's test **Unordered list** on Shopping original at blank line: already on Single at EOF \"- gamma\" correct, maybe enough.\n\nTest **Indent toolbar width** at 4: after restoring 4, tap Indent on blank line yields 4 spaces. We already tested 8 and 1 but not 4. Could verify to ensure setting reset. Use Shopping original; could create temporary blank line and indent, then reload. But we'd need disable autoformat. Instead can use Notes perhaps. Not necessary.\n\nTest **tab width dialog cancel**: Long press Indent, choose 8 then dialog closes; then choose Cancel should not change. We know 8/1 direct. Good.\n\nTest **tab width persistence after rotation** maybe. Let's do quickly with Notes: choose 8, rotate, choose 1? We already rotated while width 8? We changed to 1 in landscape then 4. Not after rotation. But area covers device rotation; not central.\n\nMaybe display **tab width** actually applied directly: we should verify an *open* editor uses new width immediately **without reopening**, which we did (8 and 1). Pass.\n\nNow preview view mode state:\n- File list opens last mode. We saw Notes initially opens preview after previous preview. Is that intended? It might be a bug: Opening a file after previously closing in view mode always opens in view mode; probably expected \"last used mode\" setting. Could check setting \"View Mode\" maybe not.\n- Back from preview returns browser, not editor. Could be expected.\n- Search in preview closing back returns browser, not preview. We saw pressing back from search returned browser; is that a navigation bug? Sequence: preview -> search icon -> type -> back hides keyboard -> back exits search **and the file entirely to browser**, skipping preview. That's possibly a bug in view mode navigation. In many apps, back from search should close search and return to preview, not browser. But maybe second back after keyboard hide triggers Markor's fragment back -> browser, closing search+preview. The first back hides keyboard, second triggers root back. It did. Expected maybe close search first. Is that part of area \"file preview and view mode\"? Could be. But not related to changed features. The task doesn't say only changed features; sweep area. Should consider. However \"when preview search is open, back should return to preview\" is a UX expectation, but not necessarily. Developer might confirm? We can test normal edit search behavior: opening search in editor and pressing back maybe exits to browser too. If consistent, it's app design. Not a bug.\n\nNeed prioritize see", "truncated": true}
