{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good.\n\nNow decide whether to sign off or continue. We have one confirmed bug (enumeration). Two unconfirmed reports. There might be remaining bugs in preview styling (copy button) not confirmed by dev, but as QA we believe it's real. Task says \"When you believe the areas above have no remaining bugs, sign off.\" We don't believe preview has no bugs. Need perhaps find/confirm more. Could sign off with note that unconfirmed? But sign_off requires verdict PASS and confidence. It says signing off while bugs remain worst. We should not sign off if we believe copy invisible is a bug. Need maybe get it confirmed somehow by another report or find alternative manifestation.\n\nMaybe our copy button bug is due **theme**? Let's inspect default theme maybe custom. Could be a screenshot rendering issue with MaterialButton icon/text because the \"Copy\" button is shown only on focus? But user-visible initial blank circle is bad. Let's try reproducing using a *save* workflow with code block in an existing file and reopening via file browser, not toggling preview. Maybe the Copy button appears correctly after a full reopen? We can test:\n- Open Single, edit to code block, Save? Press Save 712 then back, reopen (last mode edit) then preview. The copy button blank still. But maybe not.\n- Could test on a **different code block language**, e.g., no language or `js`, maybe button blank only with java? Unlikely.\n- Could test code block at different position or multiple code blocks; perhaps only first block copy button blank? Could be a clue. Our code block was single. If two code blocks, maybe both blank or second visible?\n- Could test if code block copy button becomes visible on scroll or rotate. It remained blank after rotation. It becomes visible after tap.\n- Could test if tapping **Edit Mode** then **View Mode** immediately (without other actions) results blank. We did.\n- Could test on **dark theme** to see if blank persists; if visible in dark, it's a contrast bug in light.\n- Could test **light theme vs system**. Device likely light.\n\nMaybe `Copy` button's initial icon is a **white circle with a black copy icon** but our screenshot may not capture due anti-aliasing? Looking at screenshot, blank circle clearly no black icon. Could be icon rendered in background color #F8F7F4 (same as code block), a tint bug. Tapping changes button background gray + text yellow, making it visible. This is exactlystyle issue.\n\nWhy developer couldn't reproduce? Maybe because they are using an emulator/theme where button is visible. But same app. Could our device font/resourcing? Hmm.\n\nLet's try to file again with more direct steps and maybe observed_quote from accessibility \"Copy\" might not be on screen initially. But the report expected missing, quote absent. Could the report have been rejected because `observed_quote` omitted? The instruction says \"a report about something missing may leave the quote out, but a quote that was never on screen gets the report rejected.\" It returned \"could not reproduce\", so maybe not rejected but no confirmation. Maybe we can include `observed_quote` \"Copy\" by noting that after tapping it appears. Not showing defect though.\n\nMaybe field \"Code block Copy control\" and symptom \"missing\" then dev searched for element and found it (accessibility), so couldn't reproduce invisibility. Need describe contrast: \"The Copy control is present but its label/icon is invisible (white on white).\" Symptom type could be \"wrong_value\" or \"overlap\"? It's a contrast/styling bug; available symptom types: wrong_value, missing, not_persisted, cut_off, wrong_navigation, no_effect, duplicated, overlap. \"missing\" best. Developer likely couldn't repro because they checked it exists. Perhaps \"wrong_value\" with observed \"blank white circular button; no visible label\" and quote? Hmm.\n\nCould report separately that **Copy button label is invisible** with symptom `missing`, same content. Might