{"type": "thinking", "text": "Tapping back from Settings exits app! That's a possible navigation bug: Back button in Settings/Appearance should return to More (previous screen), not close the app. We noticed earlier: pressing Back from Settings went to launcher. Now toolbar Back arrow also exits app. This seems like a serious bug in navigation. But is it related to our sweep areas? Not exactly, but it's a bug we encountered. Could be due changing theme causing activity restart then back stack cleared? Wait before theme change, we pressed back from Settings and it exited to launcher. That was before? Sequence:\n- We were in Settings > Appearance, changed Theme to Dark. Then tapped back toolbar (element1) and it exited to launcher. Could be because Settings was opened from More; expected back to More. Instead launcher.\n- Now in Settings after restoring, tapped toolbar back and again exits. So reproducible navigation bug: Settings Back returns to launcher instead of More.\nCould be because the More screen is not in back stack under Settings? But UI shows Settings with Back arrow implying up navigation. Pressing back should go to More. Why exit? This is not in focus areas, but a QA sweep can report bugs outside? Task says sweep these areas; we can report. But unnecessary? It might be an existing app behavior/bug. Could be caused by theme change? No, even after theme change back to System. The Settings Activity is a separate activity with `finish()`? Back should close Settings to whichever activity (More) launched it. But if launched More in same MainActivity and Settings separate activity, back returns? Hmm.\n\nMaybe because after theme change the app's MainActivity was recreated and More screen not in back stack? But on second try after restoring System, we tapped Back arrow in Settings; it went launcher. Maybe Settings Activity finishes to MainActivity which has current tab More? Should show More, not launcher. Strange. Perhaps `Markor` main activity closed when theme changed and Settings launched as root? Wait when we changed theme to System, the activity may recreate under Settings; app restarted to file browser? But we were in Settings still. Back finishing Settings would expose MainActivity which due task state ended? Hmm.\n\nThis is a **navigation bug** not related to sweep. Could report; developer might confirm. But focus is areas; time.\n\nWe need reopen app and ensure system theme/light back. open_app."}
