sts.\nAlternatively use Notes temporary content \"x\" and indent, then back/reopen and indent again. But we can infer persistence via opening dialog maybe not shown checked. Need count.\n\nSimpler: In an open editor, set width 8. Without modifying content, leave and reopen. Then tap at end and press Indent on a blank new line? We need create blank new line; press Enter then Indent. Observe spaces. But auto-save; restore via reload after. Could use Indent.md and reload after; but reload after setting persists width. At end reset width 4.\nWe already know current width 4. Let's test with Indent.md:\n- Open Indent.md.\n- Long-press Indent (need landscape) choose 8.\n- Maybe don't insert. Back to browser (auto save no changes).\n- Reopen Indent.md, rotate landscape, long-press? We can check width by pressing End/blank? Better create new blank line and Indent, count spaces.\nCould use pressing ENTER at end -> new blank line; tap Indent -> adds spaces. If after reopen width 8, new line gets 8 spaces. This verifies persistence. Then reload original.\nBut this is a lot of steps and may be okay.\n\nAlternatively use dialog choice highlight? The dialog didn't show current selection, so no.\n\nLet's test persistence quickly if time. Open Indent.md row14, rotate landscape, long-press Indent -> 8. Then back browser, reopen, rotate maybe orientation persists landscape or rotates; press End? We'll do simplified:\n- Open Indent.md (editor).\n- Tap Rotate to landscape.\n- Long-press Indent 24 choose 8.\n- Tap Edit? no. Hide? back to browser.\n- Reopen Indent.md.\n- Press END maybe cursor end; press ENTER new blank line; long? Tap Indent (toolbar expanded if landscape?) Reopen orientation maybe remains landscape; if not, rotate.\n- Count spaces from observe.\n\nBut we don't want to accidentally alter data beyond reload. We can reload original after.\n\nThis might uncover a real bug. Let's do."}
